  "result": "I fixed it in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. With an open bound, the clamped value came out outside the allowed range.\n\nThe cause was the sign. A value below an open `min` was clamped to `min - 1`, and a value above an open `max` to `max + 1`. It now moves inward (`bound + dir`), landing on `min + 1` or `max - 1`. For example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` now turns `-5` into `1` instead of `-1`.\n\nClosed bounds were already correct, and `FloatRange` doesn't allow clamping on open bounds, so it wasn't affected.\n\n`tests/test_types.py` passes (41 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't add a regression test for the open-bound case.",
